DESCRIPTION >
    Leads: per-visitor aggregate (first/last seen, pageview+conversion
    counts, revenue, first-touch attribution fields), any converting-or-
    active visitor. Tenant-scoped; prunes via (site_id, timestamp). Faithful
    1:1 port of api/routes/leads-server.js:41-63 (queryName 'leads_list').
    Identity rule #19a: GROUP BY distinct_id, canonical stitching key.
    Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6): properties.site_id ->
    site_id, event -> event_type, properties.utm_source -> utm_source
    (Nullable), properties.first_touch_source -> first_touch_source
    (DEFAULT 'direct'), properties.utm_medium -> utm_medium (Nullable),
    properties.first_touch_medium -> first_touch_medium (DEFAULT 'none'),
    properties.ai_source -> ai_source (Nullable), properties.country ->
    country (Nullable), properties.page_url -> page_url (Nullable),
    properties.conversion_value -> conversion_value (Float64 DEFAULT 0).
    toFloatOrZero -> toFloat64OrZero (PostHog sugar isn't a native ClickHouse
    function; same class of fix as prior batches).
    §7 NULL-SKIP ANALYSIS (per-field, done before authoring, full table in
    the batch dispatch report): argMin(source)/argMin(medium) are
    COALESCE-guarded to a non-null floor ('direct'/'none') on both the live
    HogQL bag and the typed schema, so they never actually skip — no fix
    needed. argMin(ai_source) is COALESCE-guarded to '' — same, no fix.
    argMin(country)/argMin(page_url) are genuinely Nullable typed columns
    (no DEFAULT), so ClickHouse's null-skip already matches live HogQL
    exactly — no fix needed.
    KNOWN, UNRESOLVED RESIDUAL DIVERGENCE — argMin(first_touch_campaign)
    [campaign]: this field is genuinely irreconcilable at the pipe-SQL level
    given the current schema. Cross-store testing on the gating site found
    BOTH populations exist in live (non-legacy) Tinybird data: (1)
    multi-touch/converting visitors (cc-4c-visitorY etc., routed through
    /api/track's full attribution computation) where first_touch_campaign is
    explicitly resolved to '' on every row — argMin correctly returns '' with
    no skip needed, matching live HogQL exactly; and (2) freshly-arrived,
    not-yet-attributed visitors (cc-verify-pixel-20260630a etc., single
    pageview, pre-attribution-backfill) where first_touch_campaign is
    genuinely NULL in live HogQL (verified: even ingestion_method=
    'server_routed' via /api/track can be null here) — live HogQL's argMin
    correctly skips and returns NULL, but the typed column's DEFAULT '' is
    NOT NULL so Tinybird's argMin does NOT skip, incorrectly returning ''
    instead of NULL. A nullIf(first_touch_campaign, '') fix was tried and
    made population (1) wrong instead (verified: nullIf'd cc-4c-visitorY ->
    NULL, live -> ''); NOT applying it leaves population (2) wrong (typed ->
    '', live -> NULL). Since the typed schema's null-to-default mapping has
    already destroyed the "was it genuinely absent, or explicitly set to the
    default string" distinction at ingest time, NO SQL-level choice in this
    pipe can be correct for both populations simultaneously — this is a data-
    model limitation (would need first_touch_campaign to be Nullable rather
    than DEFAULT-backed in events.datasource to fix properly), not a pipe
    bug. Left as a plain column reference (correct for the richer,
    multi-touch/converting population that is the primary use case of a
    leads list); the divergence for not-yet-attributed single-pageview
    visitors is flagged, not hidden.
    SEPARATE, FIXED issue — argMaxIf(conversion_type, ..., event_type =
    '$conversion') [last_conversion_type]: when a visitor has ZERO
    conversions (a legitimate, common case here since the HAVING clause
    admits pageview-only leads), ClickHouse's argMaxIf returns the column
    type's default ('' for String) rather than NULL — confirmed empirically
    (cc-verify-pixel-20260630a, 0 conversions: typed argMaxIf -> '', live
    HogQL -> NULL). This is a distinct, general ClickHouse-vs-HogQL
    conditional-aggregate-over-empty-set behavior, unrelated to the §2.6
    DEFAULT-column issue above. Fixed with nullIf(argMaxIf(...), '') — safe
    because every real $conversion event on the gating site has a genuine
    non-empty conversion_type (that site's data at verification time held
    closed_won/lead_created/purchase, never '' — a point-in-time observation,
    NOT the taxonomy: api/lib/conversion-classifier.js is the full list and it
    also carries the Stripe lifecycle types trial_start/trial_converted/
    subscription plus renewal/churn). The safety argument does not depend on
    WHICH values occur, only that none is '' — so new types strengthen it
    rather than weakening it, and there's no legitimate '' value this could
    wrongly clobber.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.
    DEPLOY FIX (tb --cloud deploy --check, ST_Staging v4.6.4): date/datetime
    params were declared String(param, required=True) then wrapped in
    toDateTime(...) — that combination failed with CANNOT_PARSE_DATETIME
    under --check's '__no_value__' placeholder injection (a non-date string
    toDateTime() can't parse). Fixed by declaring the param itself as
    DateTime(...) (matching the already-shipped Phase 4 pipes' proven
    pattern) and dropping the now-redundant toDateTime(...) wrapper — no
    SQL/filter logic changed, only the param type. Re-validated via
    tb --cloud sql with real values post-fix; parity held (see batch
    dispatch report).

NODE leads_list_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        distinct_id,
        MIN(timestamp) AS first_seen,
        MAX(timestamp) AS last_seen,
        countIf(event_type = '$pageview') AS pageviews,
        countIf(event_type = '$conversion' AND lower(coalesce(conversion_type, '')) != 'refund') AS conversions,
        SUM(CASE WHEN event_type = '$conversion' THEN toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)) ELSE 0 END) AS total_revenue,
        argMin(COALESCE(NULLIF(utm_source, ''), NULLIF(first_touch_source, ''), 'direct'), timestamp) AS source,
        argMin(COALESCE(NULLIF(utm_medium, ''), NULLIF(first_touch_medium, ''), 'none'), timestamp) AS medium,
        argMin(first_touch_campaign, timestamp) AS campaign,
        argMin(COALESCE(NULLIF(ai_source, ''), ''), timestamp) AS ai_source,
        argMin(country, timestamp) AS country,
        argMin(page_url, timestamp) AS first_page_url,
        nullIf(argMaxIf(conversion_type, timestamp, event_type = '$conversion'), '') AS last_conversion_type
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      {% if defined(date_from_ts) %}
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from_ts, '1970-01-01 00:00:00') }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to_ts, '1970-01-01 00:00:00') }}
      {% end %}
    GROUP BY distinct_id
    HAVING conversions > 0 OR pageviews > 0
    ORDER BY last_seen DESC
    LIMIT {{ Int32(limit_val, 50) }}
    OFFSET {{ Int32(offset_val, 0) }}

TYPE endpoint
